<div class="page">
  <header class="page-header">
    <h1><span class="h1-icon" aria-hidden="true">🔬</span>Research</h1>
    <p class="lede">I like problems where the thing you're looking for barely shows up in the data: a person who is a few pixels wide in a thermal image, a ship behind haze, one tree in a forest of point clouds. Most of this work happened in the PRISM research group at NIT Rourkela with Dr. Sobhan Kanti Dhara.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2 id="in-plain-words">In plain words</h2>
    <p>Object detectors are great at finding big, clear things. They struggle when the object is tiny, low-contrast, or surrounded by clutter, and they're usually too heavy to run on a drone. My M.Tech thesis, <em>Deep Learning Architectures for Tiny Human Detection in Aerial Thermal Imagery</em>, tackled both problems at once: four lightweight architectures (SAPNet, TSRNet, CGANet and C2SNet), each fixing a different weak spot in the usual backbone → neck → detector pipeline.</p>
  </div>

